The current implementation is "D3a" — a two-phase compromise (parallel
entity tick + serial collision_flush), not the full three-phase design
in arch §6.2 (detection / impulse / position).

Updated EntityCollisionPipeline javadoc to:
- explicitly call out which §6.2 invariants we DO match (impulse ordering,
  per-entity parallelism)
- explicitly call out which we do NOT match (detection is not a separate
  read-only phase; position update is not a separate phase)
- note the visible consequence: impulses settle one tick later than
  vanilla, which causes replay hash divergence unless the recorder also
  defers — tracked as part of B1's full determinism work.

The "D3b" full three-phase pipeline requires splitting Entity.move and
CollisionUtil; deferred to a separate workstream.

No code change — documentation only.

